1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting
sun over the Naka River,

2
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble,
and my shoe went flying too.

3
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:32,960
Right onto the head of the
carpenter who'd been saving up,

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,120
they laughed that I'm still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I chase after some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,040
in Katsushika Kameari,
even a yawn goes unused.

7
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,120
From the pointy-hat's water bottle,

9
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,440
the sun sets toward the café.

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow, too,
it'll end just like this, won't it?

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,000
In Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness gets lost again.

12
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,480
Because I'm a fool who only
realized it after hearing it.

13
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:52,240
Mm.

14
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,200
On patrol?

15
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,880
Thanks for your hard work.

16
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:01,160
Did the New Year's soba sell out?

17
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,600
Thanks to you, yes.

18
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:06,000
Reiko came by earlier too,
buying some for everyone.

19
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:06,660
I see.

20
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:09,340
I'll head back to the
police box and grab some.

21
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:10,520
See you, old man.

22
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:11,720
The year is finally...

23
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:12,320
You too, old man.

24
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:16,040
Good work.

25
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:18,440
This year's almost over

26
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:21,120
Shabu shabu, shabu shabu.

27
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:21,780
Good work.

28
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:23,560
Welcome back, Ryo-san.

29
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:27,660
Perfect timing!
Let's all eat New Year's soba together.

30
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:31,960
Nakagawa, we've been waiting!
Here's the New Year's soba, let's eat!

31
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:32,660
Yes.

32
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:38,580
Let's eat.

33
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,540
That old man's really good, isn't he?

34
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:43,940
As expected of Tanaka-san.

35
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,840
Looks like we'll somehow make
it through the year after all.

36
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,480
What are you going to do?

37
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:52,340
Dantan always holds the New
Year's party at the Chief's house.

38
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:56,200
I'm supposed to get a whole
year's worth of nutrition there.

39
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,020
The New Year's party is canceled.

40
00:02:58,020 --> 00:02:58,980
What?

41
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:02,020
I heard the Chief went to the hot
springs until the third of January.

42
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:03,700
He went out yesterday, you know.

43
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:05,860
Dirty rat! He ran off on us!

44
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:08,940
So we won't get a whole year's
worth of nutrition next year

45
00:03:08,940 --> 00:03:18,420
Shuu shuu shuu shuu shuu

46
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:21,380
A New Year without Ryotsu is the best!

47
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:24,460
Paradise, paradise.

48
00:03:25,180 --> 00:03:30,180
Hey, the chief's trying to have all the fun for himself.
Is that his scheme?

49
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:33,120
Which hot spring did the chief go to?

50
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:35,160
He did say Nikko, though.

51
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:38,180
Right, I'll search every
inn in Nikko one by one.

52
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,880
Senpai, please don't do anything rash.

53
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,260
Hey, spill it, Nakagawa.

54
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:47,180
Our kinton and herring roe were turned into money for his trip,
you know!

55
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:53,080
Make the chief realize what happens when
he treats his subordinates like that.

56
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:54,180
Spill it.

57
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:54,940
Ryo-sama

58
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:58,600
Well, if you don't mind my house...

59
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:02,040
What, your house is having
a New Year's party too?

60
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:06,680
Yes, it's a New Year's party combined
with a training camp at my father's dojo.

61
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:08,320
If that's all right with you.

62
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:09,280
Really?

63
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:14,180
Yes, my mother is a cooking expert,
so I think you'll enjoy the food.

64
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,380
Reiko-san is...

65
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:18,900
Would you all like to join us?

66
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:20,620
Are we really allowed to come too?

67
00:04:20,620 --> 00:04:23,120
Yes, may I come along too?

68
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:26,280
Because I thought there would be a
New Year's party at the chief's house.

69
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:28,480
I didn't make any plans for New Year's.

70
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:30,040
Me neither.

71
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,040
Alright, let's go, let's go!

72
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:36,420
Tomorrow's New Year's party, we're being
treated at Nakagawa's old man's training camp!

73
00:04:58,840 --> 00:04:59,880
What an extreme method.

74
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:04,520
The training camp is at
the top of the stairs.

75
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:07,760
It really feels like a
swordsmanship training camp.

76
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:08,700
Yeah, it does.

77
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:10,540
Are we really climbing this?

78
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:11,560
Of course we are.

79
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:14,180
If we don't climb, we won't get to
eat Kyoko-san's home cooking, will we?

80
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:23,160
What on earth is this stone staircase for?

81
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,660
There are 1,990 steps.

82
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:29,400
Just going up and down
this would be good training.

83
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:32,360
Someone's lying there!

84
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:35,360
This does seem like a pretty
grueling training camp.

85
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,780
Hey, hey.

86
00:05:37,620 --> 00:05:38,820
Are you all right? Snap out of it!

87
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:41,360
Damn, it reeks of booze.

88
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:44,380
They're just drunk and passed out,
these people.

89
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:47,040
What kind of training camp are they running,
I wonder?

90
00:05:47,300 --> 00:05:50,300
Sorry about that.
After all, it's bookshelf swordsmanship.

91
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:14,820
At least they're doing proper training,
aren't they?

92
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,520
Wassup! Wassup!

93
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:18,580
Wassup! Wassup!

94
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:20,400
Y-you're Coach Iwatetsu!

95
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:22,400
How dare you show your face again!

96
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:23,680
It's Coach Iwatetsu!

97
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:24,640
It's Iwatetsu Iwao!

98
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:26,940
You lot are persistent every single time.

99
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:28,560
I'm not Iwatetsu!

100
00:06:28,940 --> 00:06:30,340
It's Kankichi Ryotsu, damn it!

101
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:31,380
That's right!

102
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,420
No more talking! Prepare yourself!

103
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:37,420
Ow that hurts!

104
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,820
M-Maria!

105
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:44,060
I won't forgive anyone who commits
violence against either of you.

106
00:06:44,060 --> 00:06:46,000
You really went and did it, didn't you.

107
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:53,840
Alright, who's next?

108
00:06:53,840 --> 00:07:09,140
No matter how many of you gang up on her,
you can't win.

109
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:12,580
Lousy pervert. That's not a woman.

110
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:15,983
She may look like a woman,
but her true identity is -

111
00:07:16,033 --> 00:07:18,620
my son, Asato Ai.

112
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,900
This is the master, Ai-sama!?

113
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:24,340
In just one year, he became a woman.

114
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:26,600
Oh my God, you idiot.

115
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,740
Is this really the Ai-sama?

116
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,080
Unbelievable.

117
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,260
Beautiful.

118
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:39,600
Even my own son has returned to his father's side.
I'm glad.

119
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:41,420
It's not like that, Father.

120
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:44,340
We invited everyone from the police
box and came to the New Year's party.

121
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,300
What?

122
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:47,800
I see, Ban-chan.

123
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:50,040
We just came to eat the food.

124
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:53,820
You came to eat the food, you say?

125
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:55,520
What nonsense.

126
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:58,760
Don't let them get past!

127
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:02,456
Ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,

128
00:08:02,506 --> 00:08:04,752
Ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,
ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,

129
00:08:04,802 --> 00:08:07,025
Ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,
ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,

130
00:08:07,075 --> 00:08:09,347
Ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,
ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,

131
00:08:09,397 --> 00:08:11,607
Ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,
ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,

132
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:13,917
Ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,
ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,

133
00:08:13,967 --> 00:08:16,203
Ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,
ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,

134
00:08:16,253 --> 00:08:18,620
Ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya,
ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya, ya

135
00:08:18,620 --> 00:08:20,240
Don't be so cruel to us!

136
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,880
I'm weak when a woman starts crying to me.

137
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:31,400
Wait, come to think of it,
you're my son after all.

138
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:32,720
Papa, please.

139
00:08:33,260 --> 00:08:36,680
"Papa"? I'm weak to that word too.

140
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:39,680
Stop it.

141
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,640
Fine, I'll forgive you.

142
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:43,280
Really, Father?

143
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:47,540
But in exchange for letting
you join the New Year's party,

144
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:50,260
you'll be treated the same
as Monte and the others.

145
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:51,220
Is that really okay?

146
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:53,145
Damn it,

147
00:08:53,195 --> 00:08:56,840
why did we have to dress
like this just to learn kendo?

148
00:08:56,840 --> 00:09:00,040
All I wanted was to eat
Kyoko-san's delicious feast.

149
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:02,800
It's turned into a
training camp or something.

150
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:05,420
Holding the New Year's party at the
Chief's house would have been better.

151
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:06,540
You've changed, then.

152
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,820
We're starting the training right away.

153
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:10,100
First,

154
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:14,380
run up and down the stone steps 30 times.

155
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:19,240
When that's done, you'll go up
and down once more doing bunny hops.

156
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:19,820
That's ridiculous.

157
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,060
No arguments.

158
00:09:22,060 --> 00:09:23,280
Hurry up and go.

159
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:29,440
There's no way we can do thirty
round trips up these stone stairs.

160
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,960
I'm done for.

161
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:34,660
Getting to eat anything is going to be a real ordeal,
isn't it, senpai.

162
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:37,400
I feel like Maria tricked us somehow.

163
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:41,740
You all don't have to go all the way down.

164
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:43,940
What do you mean?

165
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:45,380
That's fine.

166
00:09:48,600 --> 00:09:52,360
Twenty, eight, twenty, nine, thirty, ori!

167
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:57,420
If we'd used one step as three steps,
it would have been a round trip, but...

168
00:09:58,060 --> 00:09:59,600
Since when is that allowed?!

169
00:09:59,980 --> 00:10:01,460
Because it's full of idiots.

170
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:04,060
So what about round trips of bunny hops?

171
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:08,956
4, 4, 4, 4,

172
00:10:09,006 --> 00:10:10,859
4, 4,

173
00:10:10,909 --> 00:10:14,240
4, 4, 4, 4

174
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:18,080
Hey, this isn't training at all!

175
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,600
Because it's all books, you know.

176
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:24,200
Ow, I've got blisters on my feet!

177
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:28,100
Damn that Hondara old man,
pulling a Little Ikkyu stunt!

178
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,260
Did someone call me?

179
00:10:31,220 --> 00:10:32,460
I'm right here.

180
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:34,800
Elgapper, you tricked me, you bastard!

181
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:37,320
If you're mad, come at me!

182
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:39,320
I'll knock that bastard flat!

183
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:41,540
Lord Ryo

184
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:43,720
Idiot, there's a pitfall here!

185
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:45,623
And it's filled with dog shit, too.

186
00:10:45,673 --> 00:10:48,280
Now you've really gone and done it,
you bastard.

187
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:50,300
Hey, don't act like a brat!

188
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:54,500
Our Honden Kenpo training
camps always come with a catch.

189
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:57,260
A catch, you say? Fall in!

190
00:10:58,460 --> 00:11:01,140
Honden Kenpo muscle-strengthening
special training, ready!

191
00:11:01,380 --> 00:11:01,800
Ugh!

192
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:06,960
That iron girder weighs
two tons on each side.

193
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:07,860
T-two tons?

194
00:11:08,060 --> 00:11:09,720
You don't mean we have
to shoulder that girder?

195
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:12,440
Like this.
I call it the Iron Girder Grit Training!

196
00:11:12,920 --> 00:11:13,440
Go!

197
00:11:18,220 --> 00:11:20,020
Having put on 2-ton steel girders,

198
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,620
So, what are we doing?

199
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:23,920
Wearing 2-ton steel girders,

200
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:28,160
we're hanging out the laundry.

201
00:11:28,820 --> 00:11:30,840
What's the point of wearing steel girders?

202
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,780
A bookshelf sword?

203
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:35,200
It's too early to be surprised.

204
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:37,960
Next, Bookshelf Sword Art:
Alanio's Ultimate Secret!

205
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:39,240
Sorry if I die.

206
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,740
Hellish cold wind special training!

207
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:41,760
Begin!

208
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:43,120
Yo.

209
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:50,020
Stripped down to nothing
in the bitter winter wind,

210
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:54,440
we soak in a hot spring,

211
00:11:56,100 --> 00:11:57,560
and then we drink sake!

212
00:11:58,020 --> 00:12:00,820
What hell? That's paradise, if you ask me!

213
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:03,440
There's always a catch in this world.

214
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:05,060
Don't screw with me!

215
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:07,020
And I don't need a punchline, thanks.

216
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:09,840
You're the one who came here to mess around,
jackass!

217
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:11,400
Just kill me.

218
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:18,540
What the hell are you doing?

219
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,940
Idiot, you nearly died!

220
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:23,000
We've stirred up a hornet's nest!

221
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,420
We've really stirred up a hornet's nest!

222
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:25,860
Ryo-san, are you all right?

223
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,740
A duel challenge!

224
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:35,900
Even if it's morning...

225
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,140
Me?

226
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:41,900
I'll settle this someday!
I'm waiting, Fūdai Zaimon!

227
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:44,060
Fūdai Zaimon

228
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:45,280
You know him?

229
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:49,200
Fūdai Zaimon...
I've heard that name somewhere.

230
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:54,240
What is this wind?

231
00:13:12,400 --> 00:13:15,240
This dramatic entrance
with the wind behind it

232
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:16,840
Ah

233
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:32,640
Don't stir up wind with an electric fan!

234
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:34,360
Who are you?

235
00:13:36,100 --> 00:13:38,340
Is this a lone fight?

236
00:13:38,340 --> 00:13:41,340
Kase, the great sinner!

237
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:41,960
What?

238
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,140
You're the one...

239
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:44,900
Kase.

240
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:47,300
Where's Ai Asato?

241
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,400
Where's Ai Asato?

242
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:08,360
Are you the Sympathy Breaker?

243
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:09,720
We are your opponents.

244
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:11,620
We have no business with small fry.

245
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:13,840
What, who are you calling small fry?

246
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:14,620
Unforgivable!

247
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:35,320
Seriously?

248
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:35,880
Look!

249
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:37,060
Hahahaha!

250
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,900
How about that! Clear the way!

251
00:14:41,140 --> 00:14:42,860
Lighting a fire all of a sudden...

252
00:14:42,860 --> 00:14:45,340
W-wait!
I won't let you lay a finger on the sauce!

253
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:48,540
Heh heh.
Get close to me and you're in danger.

254
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:51,700
Come on, who's next!
Who wants to become a spirit daruma!

255
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,040
Stop it!

256
00:14:57,420 --> 00:14:58,060
Go!

257
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:21,440
!

258
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:22,580
He's a self-taught master.

259
00:15:22,580 --> 00:15:23,740
Self-taught?

260
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:25,700
I remember now.

261
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:26,640
That face.

262
00:15:26,640 --> 00:15:29,080
He's the guy who fought Ai in
the martial arts tournament.

263
00:15:29,080 --> 00:15:29,640
Yeah, that's right.

264
00:15:31,500 --> 00:15:32,780
I'll never forget it.

265
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:36,900
The final of the world martial
arts championship three years ago.

266
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,220
Asato and I

267
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:42,140
fought for the title of
world's greatest martial artist.

268
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:49,260
Ai!

269
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:51,560
Yes! This one's on a different
level from the opponents so far!

270
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,480
Use the Bookshelf Sword technique!

271
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:54,700
But...

272
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:55,700
Yes!

273
00:15:58,260 --> 00:15:59,860
Shut up! Come on, come on!

274
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:01,380
What are you doing!

275
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:04,640
Use the Monkey Dance! The Monkey Dance!

276
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:08,040
Now!

277
00:16:10,380 --> 00:16:11,180
What!?

278
00:16:20,620 --> 00:16:22,780
Knockout! The winner is Ai Asato!

279
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:24,960
Yeah! Well done, Ai!

280
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:30,740
I'll never forget that humiliation.

281
00:16:32,260 --> 00:16:33,516
Three years have passed since then,

282
00:16:33,566 --> 00:16:37,300
and I've trained with my life on the line,
sharpening my skills.

283
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:40,160
And whenever I felt like giving up,

284
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:45,514
I'd look at Asato's
photo and renew my hatred,

285
00:16:45,564 --> 00:16:47,100
and keep pushing myself through training.

286
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:51,700
You know, normally you'd keep a
picture of your lover in a locket.

287
00:16:51,700 --> 00:16:54,480
Shut up!
I'll show you the results of my training.

288
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:02,860
Asato's favorite strike from above,

289
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:08,360
I'll dodge it like this.

290
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,920
Ugh, hah!

291
00:17:14,180 --> 00:17:15,300
Achoo!

292
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:16,920
Seiso!

293
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:35,380
Did you see that? My own secret technique:
the Dance of the White Heron!

294
00:17:35,920 --> 00:17:39,660
Never mind the technique,
but wasn't that first shuriken a cheap move?

295
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:43,840
Shut up! To defeat the strongest Asato,
I'll use any means necessary.

296
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:46,080
Come on, Asato! Where are you?

297
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:47,480
Dogedoge!

298
00:17:49,140 --> 00:17:50,800
Where's Asato?

299
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:52,140
Wait!

300
00:17:52,480 --> 00:17:52,960
Y-yes!

301
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:55,560
Where's Asato?

302
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:58,020
Asato!

303
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,600
I'm right here...

304
00:18:02,600 --> 00:18:04,540
Don't say a word, dogee!

305
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:07,000
Asato.

306
00:18:10,040 --> 00:18:11,640
That's why I'm here.

307
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:12,920
What a persistent woman.

308
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,340
Asato!

309
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:15,960
Asato!

310
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,480
Asato!

311
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,020
Asato!

312
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:27,720
Beautiful.

313
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:29,420
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

314
00:18:29,420 --> 00:18:30,020
Yes.

315
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:33,080
Is there anyone who barges into
someone's home with their shoes on?

316
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:37,220
My apologies, excuse me.

317
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,380
Haha, hello.

318
00:18:39,640 --> 00:18:41,660
Ah, Kyoko-san.

319
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,480
Ryotsu-san.

320
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:45,840
Hello, happy New Year.

321
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:47,180
Happy New Year.

322
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:49,420
Yes, please look after me again this year.

323
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:50,660
Likewise.

324
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:53,736
Hey, Fūdai Zaimon.

325
00:18:53,786 --> 00:18:56,940
The Asato Ai you're looking for is this guy.

326
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:58,840
Don't joke around!

327
00:19:01,620 --> 00:19:03,380
This is serious!

328
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:05,860
What!?

329
00:19:06,300 --> 00:19:08,440
Don't be cruel to Ryo-sama!

330
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:11,400
That masterful block... could it be?!

331
00:19:11,860 --> 00:19:13,820
That guy really is Ai Asato.

332
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:16,040
That's impossible!

333
00:19:20,300 --> 00:19:22,300
Is this really the real Asato?

334
00:19:22,720 --> 00:19:23,080
Yes.

335
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:26,935
Ai fell for Iwatetsu Takachi a year ago,

336
00:19:26,985 --> 00:19:29,720
and ended up becoming a woman.

337
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:59,060
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

338
00:19:59,820 --> 00:20:01,220
That's too pitiful.

339
00:20:01,220 --> 00:20:03,860
After three years of mountain training,

340
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:06,380
that's the harsh reality
of the competitive world.

341
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:07,220
Where exactly?

342
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:08,080
Everyone,

343
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:10,460
perfect timing.

344
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:12,780
Dinner's ready.

345
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:14,020
We've been waiting!

346
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:17,400
Mom has put her heart into this shishi nabe.

347
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:19,720
Senpai, we're finally going to get to eat.

348
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:22,620
Thanks to that bastard,
I'd completely forgotten.

349
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:26,040
We came here for the New Year's
party meal in the first place!

350
00:20:28,140 --> 00:20:28,860
Itadakimasu.

351
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:39,160
It's a shishi-nabe with wild mountain
vegetables picked from this mountain.

352
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:41,740
It's fresh and really delicious.

353
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:44,040
As expected of a cooking researcher's taste.

354
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:47,520
There's plenty, so please help yourselves.

355
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:50,560
Meat beats vegetables. Meat is the best!

356
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:54,220
Here, take mine, then talk.

357
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:57,100
I love meat too, so talk!

358
00:20:57,100 --> 00:20:59,420
Old folks should stick to eating vegetables!

359
00:20:59,540 --> 00:21:00,560
What did you say, you little...!

360
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:01,640
Wait, this is...

361
00:21:01,690 --> 00:21:05,240
It's the same setup as last year's
New Year party at the Chief's house.

362
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:07,440
I've got a bad feeling about this.

363
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,980
Hey, you! I told you to talk!

364
00:21:10,260 --> 00:21:10,740
Nooo!

365
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:12,020
Wow!

366
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:14,460
Ryo-sama, are you all right?

367
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:14,780
Oishoi!

368
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:17,000
Father!

369
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:20,260
It's his fault. Learn a little restraint.

370
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:23,060
So it's you!

371
00:21:23,340 --> 00:21:27,280
Sorry for making you feed me by hand,
Ban-chan.

372
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:29,700
You, don't you dare.

373
00:21:30,480 --> 00:21:31,780
Take this, bookshelf sword!

374
00:21:32,080 --> 00:21:32,420
Are you coming?

375
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:34,540
Spit dance!

376
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:40,640
I see right through your
bookshelf sword tricks.

377
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:42,420
You there, give back the pot!

378
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:43,620
Hehe, nyah-nyah.

379
00:21:45,260 --> 00:22:06,020
Hey, Ban-chan, waaaaaaaaaaaaait!

380
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:08,780
I've become a woman too, you know.

381
00:22:08,780 --> 00:22:11,480
Now it's a fair fight, Asato!

382
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:13,700
No, that's disgusting.

383
00:22:14,220 --> 00:22:16,740
I won't waste my three years of training,
not for anything.

384
00:22:16,740 --> 00:22:18,200
Come on, bring it on.

385
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:21,200
I told you, no shoes allowed!

386
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:23,900
I'm sorry.

387
00:22:26,020 --> 00:22:27,160
How unlike me.

388
00:22:29,040 --> 00:22:30,280
What do you think you're doing?

389
00:22:30,280 --> 00:22:33,280
If you make a mess, you clean it up.
Obviously.

390
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:35,240
Fine, I get it.

391
00:22:36,020 --> 00:22:36,380
Yeah.

392
00:22:36,700 --> 00:22:37,900
Move! Move! Move! Move!

393
00:22:38,300 --> 00:22:39,040
Move!

394
00:22:39,240 --> 00:22:39,680
No way!

395
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:41,080
Nooo!

396
00:22:41,580 --> 00:22:42,340
No way!

397
00:22:42,580 --> 00:22:43,240
Nooo!

398
00:22:44,340 --> 00:22:46,640
You've wasted a whole pot!

399
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:48,900
There are still plenty of pots!

400
00:22:49,220 --> 00:22:49,820
Wait!

401
00:22:50,740 --> 00:22:51,620
Wait!

402
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:53,320
I did it too

403
00:22:53,860 --> 00:22:55,140
If you make a mess, clean it up!

404
00:22:55,580 --> 00:22:56,360
Y-yes.

405
00:22:58,040 --> 00:23:00,840
I didn't make this mess, you know.
How awful.

406
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:01,600
Out of the way! Move!

407
00:23:03,940 --> 00:23:04,620
No!

408
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:06,840
Ugh!

409
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:08,120
Ugh!

410
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,620
Wait a minute!

411
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:13,800
Hey, you! Enough already!

412
00:23:14,580 --> 00:23:15,300
Ryo-sama!

413
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:17,580
Maria!

414
00:23:17,900 --> 00:23:20,440
Eyebrow gorilla! I won't let you get away!

415
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:22,000
Asato, it's a showdown!

416
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:24,420
You're persistent! Just give up already!

417
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:25,820
No way!

418
00:23:26,540 --> 00:23:27,160
What did you say?

419
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:28,740
Whoa!

420
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:30,900
Yikes!

421
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:32,640
Ryo-sama, watch out!

422
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:36,980
Damn it!

423
00:23:41,180 --> 00:23:41,980
Watch out!

424
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:43,500
It's collapsing!

425
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,280
What's going on?

426
00:23:48,700 --> 00:23:52,580
The gag is that knocking over the
pillar makes the whole dojo collapse!

427
00:23:52,920 --> 00:23:54,940
Why would you build such a contraption?

428
00:23:55,820 --> 00:23:59,140
We don't need that kind of punchline!

429
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:16,820
They say I'm a woman who can't fall in love,

430
00:24:16,820 --> 00:24:22,480
but I have so many things I want to do, me!

431
00:24:22,480 --> 00:24:31,560
I want to ride a motorbike
across a harsh desert,

432
00:24:31,560 --> 00:24:38,700
I want to be freer than a bird.

433
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:46,660
A lady's dreams that change
as fast as a kaleidoscope,

434
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:54,580
sorry, my heart of love, I'll let you lose,

435
00:24:54,580 --> 00:25:01,700
the dazzling brilliance of
living out a panoramic future.

436
00:25:02,980 --> 00:25:06,035
You understand, right?

437
00:25:06,085 --> 00:25:09,580
Sorry, just wait for me.

